[3.214998] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Get across a riddle of wooden windmills spinning more or less faster. Timing and precision is needed for a level that is sure to spin your head (or make you go \"smh\", you choose)."
[3.215289] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "The title of the level is a rough translation of a french title of a level from King of Clubs, a mini-golf game I used to camp when I was a little bit younger, and it was on the Wii. \n \nThe title is \"Tu veux des moulins ?\" (this is also a good way to see who has the worst french accent). This level had 3 windmills, spinning faster than their predecessors, and the player had to time his putt to make a jump across a gap without being bruh\'d or slammed by a windmill.\n \nThe third windmill was particularly hard to cross, since it was spinning as fast as my washer. Now this level inspired me, and I decided, after a few experiments, to use the same design Training Wheels has. The ending originally had 5 WHOOPIN\' WINDMILLS (the one before the finish excluded) to get through on the moving platforms, and I finally thought this would be too harsh as a final challenge, so I sticked with only two, spinning at high speeds."
[3.218003] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Other considered names for this level included \"Patulous Propellers,\"\n\"Turbine Tower,\" and \"Propellinquity\" (which is a portmanteau of \'propinquity\' and \'propeller.\')\n\nA triskelion is a symbol consisting of three lines radiating from a center."
[3.219774] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "This level was supposed to be called \"Fading Madness\", but you know... name originality. Plus there\'s not many night levels in PQ (by that, I mean real dark night levels, unlike Bag of Secrets and Miscalculation). \n \nOriginally, the level was supposed to feature moving fading platforms. Here \'s three reasons why it didn\'t happened: \n \n1) The number of PathNodes would make the whole level lag violently\n \n2) I still can\'t make triggerable PathNodes systems because their linked objects don\'t stay in place until I get the marble in the PathTrigger\n \n3) When a fading platform is linked to a PathNode system, try landing on it :\nyou\'ll be bounced sideways, and that can be seriously annoying to the player. \nTry this glitch out for yourself if you want to."
[3.232610] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Make sure to grab the \"Bonus Fruit\" once it pops out in the center of the Maze!"
[3.235410] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "To get the first version of this level, take out most of the scenery, the \"vertical\" landmine dispensers, shorten the second water pool. \nFeeling that the level is bland as heck, I went \"oh gosh, it\'s so bland, let\'s throw lots of scenery!\" \nThis level has been left without updates for 5 months."
[3.237464] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "This is my first attempt at a \"construction\" themed level. How did I do?"
[3.240178] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Crionica: \"Hey, Marble! Yes, you! Either you get frozen or take a plunge in my purple poison, so give it up already! Muhahahaha!!\" *cough cough*"
[3.240279] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Boredom + the fact that it was snowing outside + idea of revisiting El Titiritero = this level. \n \nBy the way, \"Crionica\" is a translation for \"cryogenics\", from Spanish. I don\'t speak Spanish at all, but I thought a Spanish name would be cool. \n \nThe poi"
[3.241136] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Crionica: \"Hey, Marble! Yes, you! Either you get frozen or take a plunge in my purple poison, so give it up already! Muhahahaha!!\" *cough cough*"
[3.241237] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Boredom + the fact that it was snowing outside + idea of revisiting El Titiritero = this level. \n \nBy the way, \"Crionica\" is a translation for \"cryogenics\", from Spanish. I don\'t speak Spanish at all, but I thought a Spanish name would be cool. \n \nThe poison texture has been used before in an unreleased level I made in MBP, just like the poison pond in Tostarena, Super Mario Odyssey. You might see this texture again in future levels."
[3.246469] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "This level is an answer to a question I\'ve been asking myself since the release of PQ, \"Can I remake Having a Blast with sniper cannons?\", which is basically why Blasting Safari has a very similar level design with Having a Blast. \n \nFun fact: the most heavily modified part of this level is the platforming section behind the gate, and I spent 20-25 minutes to think about how it woild be played, set everything up in the Constructor and make the turntables."
[3.248094] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "I\'m a \"fan\" of this Nest Egg spot. God that pun was awful."
[3.299742] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Before this was turned into a construction-themed level, this was styled after the two \"Ascent of Peril\" levels by Xelna, with the idea of mixing the two and seeing how closely certain parts could be recreated. \n\nThis level was updated three years after creation, with checkpoints being added before being featured in Pack 8 on the leaderboards."
[3.301874] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "This level was originally a sequel to \"Cluttered Assortment\" as it\'s made up of some Marble Blast Ultra customs. However, after having built the scenery and giving the level its nature aesthetic, it was deemed a sequel to \"Hunter\'s Pursuit\"."
[3.303762] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Another one of Nockess\' old levels that was started years before completion. At first, this was a level made for Platinum and used a handful of the black and gray textures, hence the original name \"Grayscale\"."
[3.313825] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Working title for this level was \"Green Bean\". This level was driven by inspiration from old Phil custom levels."
[3.315294] getMissionInfo() :: eval: "Made as a continuation for my very very short level called \"RagingQuest\""
